; Regression: null may not be assigned to a NON-OPTIONAL reference
; (2026-08-23, the `ref[T]` consolidation, step 4).
;
; `docs/scaly/chapters/types.xml` has always reserved the nullable spelling
; `ref[T]?` for a slot that may hold nothing, and nothing enforced it: ref and
; pointer are one representation, so null flowed into either. The step-3 port
; conversion therefore carried the ports' nullability across unchanged and
; 1 018 sites began claiming a reference exists where the code stores null.
;
; The gate judges the bare `null` LITERAL against a declared `ref[T]` at the
; four positions where a target type is in hand: a typed binding, a `set`, an
; explicit `return` and the implicit tail return. The exits are the `?` form
; (null_into_ref_ok.scaly proves all four) and, where the caller has already
; proven non-null, the explicit `x as ref[T]` unwrap.
;
; xfail: null assigned to a non-optional reference

define Box (v: int)

var b Box(7)
var r: ref[Box] &b
r := null
Console.println "unreachable"
